  "activity": {
    "id": "act_heart_anatomy",
    "name": "The Human Heart: Structure and the Path of Blood",
    "description": "A guided AR laboratory in which students explore the structural anatomy of the human heart and trace the dual-loop circulation. Students identify the four chambers, four valves, and major vessels; distinguish the pulmonary from the systemic circuit; follow a red blood cell through the full path; compare left and right ventricular wall thickness; and examine how valves prevent backflow. Aligned with Human Anatomy and Physiology I learning objectives for 200-level nursing, kinesiology, and pre-health students.",
    "workplace": "wp_heart_anatomy",
    "start": "step_orientation",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_orientation",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "1. Gross Orientation of the Heart",
          "description": "Two full-size heart models appear side by side: the intact heart on the left shows the exterior surface and major vessels, while the cutaway heart on the right exposes the four chambers, septum, and valves. Rotate both together to view from any angle. Notice the apex points down and slightly left. Remember: the heart is described from the patient's orientation, so the anatomical 'right' side appears on your left. Click Next when ready."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_intact_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_orientation",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_intact_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_orientation",
              "poi": "poi_label",
              "text": "Intact Heart \u2014 Exterior & Vessels"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_orientation",
              "poi": "poi_label",
              "text": "Cutaway Heart \u2014 Interior View"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_intact_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_structural_tour"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_structural_tour",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "2. Structural Tour \u2014 Chambers, Valves, Vessels",
          "description": "Follow the guided tour on the cutaway heart. Each structure is highlighted in sequence with a label: the four chambers (right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, left ventricle); the four valves (tricuspid, pulmonary, mitral/bicuspid, aortic); and the major vessels (superior and inferior vena cava, pulmonary arteries, pulmonary veins, aorta). The matching region on the intact heart lights up so you can map interior structures to exterior landmarks. Note the mitral valve is also called the bicuspid valve. Click Next to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_structural_tour",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_highlight_structures",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_chamber",
              "poi": "poi_right_atrium",
              "text": "Right Atrium"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_valve",
              "poi": "poi_valves",
              "text": "Tricuspid \u2022 Pulmonary \u2022 Mitral \u2022 Aortic"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_intact_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_vessel",
              "poi": "poi_vessels",
              "text": "SVC \u2022 IVC \u2022 Pulmonary Arteries/Veins \u2022 Aorta"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_intact_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_dual_circuit"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_dual_circuit",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "3. Dual-Circuit Blood Flow",
          "description": "The cutaway heart fills with flowing color: blue for deoxygenated blood (right side, pulmonary arteries, systemic veins) and red for oxygenated blood (left side, pulmonary veins, systemic arteries). Watch the two loops highlight in turn \u2014 the pulmonary circuit carries blood to the lungs, and the systemic circuit carries blood to the body. The right heart pumps deoxygenated blood to the lungs; the left heart pumps oxygenated blood to the body. Click Next to trace a single cell."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_dual_circuit",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_dual_bloodstream",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_circuit",
              "poi": "poi_right_ventricle",
              "text": "Pulmonary Circuit (to lungs)"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_circuit",
              "poi": "poi_left_ventricle",
              "text": "Systemic Circuit (to body)"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_rbc_trace"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_rbc_trace",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "4. Trace a Red Blood Cell",
          "description": "A single red blood cell begins in the superior vena cava. Watch it travel step by step: right atrium \u2192 tricuspid valve \u2192 right ventricle \u2192 pulmonary valve \u2192 pulmonary trunk \u2192 pulmonary arteries \u2192 lungs (turns red as it picks up oxygen) \u2192 pulmonary veins \u2192 left atrium \u2192 mitral valve \u2192 left ventricle \u2192 aortic valve \u2192 aorta \u2192 body \u2192 and back blue through the veins to the superior vena cava. Detect the cutaway heart to confirm you are tracking the journey, then continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_rbc_trace",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_rbc_journey",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_vessel",
              "poi": "poi_right_atrium",
              "text": "Start: Superior Vena Cava \u2192 Right Atrium"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "anchor_cutaway_heart"
          },
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_wall_thickness"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_wall_thickness",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "5. Ventricular Wall Thickness",
          "description": "Two ventricular cross-sections appear at the same horizontal level. The right ventricle wall is thin (about 3-5 mm) because it pumps blood only to the low-pressure pulmonary circuit. The left ventricle wall is much thicker (about 10-15 mm) because it must pump against the high resistance of the entire systemic circuit \u2014 roughly a three-to-one thickness ratio. Rotate and compare using the scale markers. Click Next to examine the valves."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cross_sections",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_wall_thickness",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cross_sections",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_wall_thickness_diagram",
              "poi": "poi_label"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cross_sections",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_wall",
              "poi": "poi_rv_wall",
              "text": "Right Ventricle ~3-5 mm (low pressure)"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cross_sections",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_wall",
              "poi": "poi_lv_wall",
              "text": "Left Ventricle ~10-15 mm (high pressure)"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cross_sections",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_valves"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_valves",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "6. Valve Function & Backflow Prevention",
          "description": "The four valves are highlighted on the cutaway heart, each shown in open and closed states. The atrioventricular valves (tricuspid, mitral) sit between atria and ventricles and prevent backflow into the atria when ventricles contract. The semilunar valves (pulmonary, aortic) sit between ventricles and their outflow arteries and prevent backflow into the ventricles when they relax. During ventricular contraction: AV valves closed, semilunar valves open \u2014 during relaxation, the reverse. Click Next for the recap."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_valves",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "anim_valve_open_close",
              "poi": "poi_valves"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_valve",
              "poi": "poi_right_atrium",
              "text": "AV Valves: Tricuspid & Mitral"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "label_valve",
              "poi": "poi_left_ventricle",
              "text": "Semilunar Valves: Pulmonary & Aortic"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_cutaway_heart",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_recap"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_recap",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "7. Lab Recap",
          "description": "Review the five concept areas covered in this lab: (1) the structural inventory of chambers, valves, and vessels; (2) the dual-circuit organization of pulmonary and systemic circulation; (3) the path of a unit of blood through the full circuit; (4) the wall thickness asymmetry between the left and right ventricles; and (5) the function of valves in preventing backflow. Each area is highlighted as the narration reviews it. Click to finish the lab."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_summary_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "narration_recap",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_summary_board",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "img_recap_summary",
              "poi": "poi_content"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_summary_board",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_recap"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
